     "t": "code",
     "lang": "python",
     "code": "\"\"\"\nMRO (METHOD RESOLUTION ORDER)\n================================\n\nMRO is the order in which Python searches classes for a method.\nUses C3 Linearization algorithm (see Q150 for detailed algorithm).\n\nKey rules:\n  1. Child before parent\n  2. Parents in definition order (left to right)\n  3. Each class appears only once\n  4. Consistent ordering: if A before B in one path, A before B in MRO\n\nAccess: cls.__mro__ or cls.mro()\nsuper() follows MRO, not direct parent hierarchy.\n\"\"\"\n\nprint(\"Q161: MRO (see Q150 for detailed C3 linearization)\")\nprint(f\"  int MRO: {[c.__name__ for c in int.__mro__]}\")\nprint(f\"  bool MRO: {[c.__name__ for c in bool.__mro__]}\")\nprint()",
     "numbered": false
