     "t": "code",
     "lang": "python",
     "code": "\"\"\"\nSTATIC METHODS\n===============\n\n@staticmethod: a method that doesn't receive 'self' or 'cls'.\n  - Belongs to the class namespace but is independent of instances\n  - Cannot access or modify instance or class state\n  - Essentially a regular function inside a class\n\nUse when:\n  - The method is logically related to the class\n  - But doesn't need access to self or cls\n  - Utility/helper functions\n\"\"\"\n\n\nclass MathUtils:\n    @staticmethod\n    def add(a, b):\n        return a + b\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_even(n):\n        return n % 2 == 0\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def factorial(n):\n        if n <= 1:\n            return 1\n        return n * MathUtils.factorial(n - 1)\n\n\ndef demo_static_methods():\n    print(f\"  MathUtils.add(3, 4) = {MathUtils.add(3, 4)}\")\n    print(f\"  MathUtils.is_even(7) = {MathUtils.is_even(7)}\")\n    print(f\"  MathUtils.factorial(5) = {MathUtils.factorial(5)}\")\n\n    # Can also call on instance (unusual but works)\n    m = MathUtils()\n    print(f\"  m.add(1, 2) = {m.add(1, 2)}\")\n\n\nprint(\"Q164: Static Methods\")\ndemo_static_methods()\nprint()",
